  v_n0["When cache#95; exists and the <br/>device is not Stopping, <br/>queueBuffer calls get. <br/>Neither error newly <br/>registers this buffer in <br/>queuedBuffers#95;."]
  v_n1{"get returns -ENOENT if it <br/>cannot select an available <br/>cache entry. At that point, <br/>there is no guard or <br/>acquired index."}
  v_n2{"The common validation <br/>returns -EINVAL if the <br/>number of planes is smaller <br/>than the device format <br/>requires."}
  v_n3{"The isContiguous check <br/>tests contiguity when the <br/>number of planes differs <br/>from the format count and <br/>returns -EINVAL if the <br/>buffer is not contiguous."}
  v_n4["On return after common <br/>validation fails, the <br/>scope#95;exit guard calls put <br/>on the acquired index, <br/>making that cache entry <br/>available again."]
  v_n5["After the common checks and <br/>remaining preliminary <br/>processing pass, <br/>VIDIOC#95;QBUF is called. <br/>Details after ioctl are <br/>outside this scope."]
  v_n6["queueRequestDevice <br/>processes controls first <br/>and returns a negative ret <br/>from queueBuffer unchanged. <br/>This path provides no <br/>guarantee that all controls <br/>are applied and shows no <br/>rollback."]
  v_n7{"doQueueRequest checks <br/>whether the return value <br/>from queueRequestDevice is <br/>nonzero."}
  v_n8["cancelRequest cancels and <br/>completes the request. The <br/>submission ordering and <br/>calling rules of <br/>completeRequest apply."]
